WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.987
Try it.

2
00:00:00.987 --> 00:00:05.938
Lab 1 runs in PowerShell 7, from the kit's
folder, on the kit's fictional estate.

3
00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:10.671
First, make this run's results folder:
its name is the time you start,

4
00:00:10.671 --> 00:00:13.563
in U T C, so every run
keeps its own results.

5
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:16.774
Step one writes sequel P
R D oh one's login plan.

6
00:00:16.774 --> 00:00:19.925
Four legacy logins map to
four Entra principals.

7
00:00:19.925 --> 00:00:23.875
The create script starts with a
dry-run comment: nothing here has run.

8
00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:27.530
Notice that S Q L dash D B A
dash Admins gets sys-admin,

9
00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.750
because the Windows
group it replaces had it.

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.312
The S A account and the built-in
service login aren't in the plan.

11
00:00:34.312 --> 00:00:39.325
Then the summary: four logins mapped, none
unresolved, and the create script's hash.

12
00:00:39.325 --> 00:00:40.712
And three warnings.

13
00:00:40.712 --> 00:00:45.005
Payroll web M I and the payroll users
group would each hold three roles,

14
00:00:45.005 --> 00:00:47.300
and the D B A group would hold sys-admin.

15
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.913
The plan is still written.

16
00:00:48.913 --> 00:00:51.342
Splitting the groups,
or recording why not,

17
00:00:51.342 --> 00:00:54.960
is the identity engineer's call
before the mapping is approved.
